<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Merv</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Merv was a great oasis city of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/central-asia">Central Asia</a>, in present-day Turkmenistan, on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/silk-road">Silk Road</a>. The last Sasanian king, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yazdegerd-iii">Yazdegerd III</a>, was killed near Merv in 651 while fleeing the Arab conquest. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seljuk-empire">Seljuks</a> captured Merv in 1037, and it later became one of the main cities of the Seljuk Empire.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/merv.jpg" alt="Merv" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Kalpak Travel · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Turkmenistan_Merv_city.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
